//? Title: StyleGAN: Explicit Styles, Learned Noise and Two Normalizations
//? Subtitle: Native AdaIN and modulated-convolution teaching runs with visible optimizer steps
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Two compact8x8 generators separate a latent mapping, per-layer styles and supplied
spatial noise. One normalizes feature maps before an affine style; the other
modulates and demodulates kernels per example. The native C++ APIs expose both
paths without hiding noise draws, truncation or optimizer updates. Small worked
examples check population moments, normalization derivatives, noise learnability
and least-squares scales before the complete editable two-trial training program.
Three fixed epochs reproduce the original trajectories and controls exactly.
The resulting images remain weak: reproducible style/noise effects and correct
training arithmetic do not establish high-quality digit generation.
)
\toc

> Separate latent mapping, per-layer styles and supplied spatial noise

[Karras, Laine and Aila, A Style-Based Generator Architecture for Generative
Adversarial Networks (CVPR2019)](https://arxiv.org/abs/1812.04948) introduced the
style-based generator. [Karras, Laine, Aittala, Hellsten, Lehtinen and Aila,
Analyzing and Improving the Image Quality of StyleGAN
(CVPR2020)](https://arxiv.org/abs/1912.04958) develops weight modulation and
demodulation. These are compact teaching variants: fixed8x8 resolution, two
8-unit mapping layers, four feature channels, least-squares objectives and a
493-value critic. There is no growth schedule, moving-average generator,
path-length penalty or full paper evaluation.

The diagram separates external inputs. Both styled feature layers read their
own supplied spatial noise, multiplied by learned per-channel strengths. W0
styles the4x4 layer, W1 the8x8 layer and, in the modulated variant, the RGB map.
Using one mapped W in both positions gives ordinary Z-only generation with
explicit noise; using different mapped vectors produces the mixing controls.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/style_method.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
