> Check population spatial normalization before adding a style

For supplied values1,3,5,7, the mean is4 and population variance5. Native
spatial_instance_normalize centers each NHWC row/channel over H,W and divides by
sqrt(variance+epsilon), with epsilon=double(float32(1e-8)). It uses live means
and variance, so derivatives include the normalization dependence. Constant
channels become zero. It has no affine parameters or moving statistics.
AdaIN then multiplies by1+scale_delta and adds shift. This example supplies
scale_delta=1 and shift=.5; it does not fit a network.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/style_spatial_toy.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  auto x      = n::tensor({1., 3., 5., 7.}, {1, 2, 2, 1}, n::DType::Float64);
  auto y      = n::spatial_instance_normalize(x);
  auto affine = y * 2. + .5;
  if (std::abs(n::mean(y).item()) > 1e-14 ||
      std::abs(n::mean(n::square(y)).item() - 5. / (5. + double(1e-8f))) > 1e-14)
    throw std::runtime_error("population moments");
  auto                p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  std::vector<double> index{0, 1, 2, 3};
  p.y_limits(-3, 6)
      .points(index, y.to_vector<double>(), "Normalized", {37, 99, 235}, 5)
      .points(index, affine.to_vector<double>(), "Gain2, shift.5", {220, 38, 38}, 5)
      .x_label("Supplied spatial position")
      .y_label("Feature value")
      .title("Population normalization followed by a separate affine style")
      .save_svg("build/style_spatial_toy.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
\image(figures/style_spatial_toy.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Four supplied spatial values produce eight plotted points. Normalization uses population variance, without a batch interaction. The affine style is separate from the reusable primitive.)
\alttext(Two four-point series compare centered normalized spatial values with gain2 and shift.5 applied afterward.)

> Keep the kernel-normalization derivative

A1x1 kernel with channel weights(3,4), gains(1,1) and input(1,0) gives
3/sqrt(25+epsilon), approximately.6. Its weight partials are approximately
(.128,-.096); stopping the demodulator would incorrectly give(.2,0).
The native primitive returns both image and live per-output demodulator.
It accepts signed and zero channel gains, odd square kernels and rectangular
NHWC images. SAME zero padding and row-major tap accumulation preserve source
Float32 grouping. The modulated RGB map sets demodulate=false, retaining the
source computed-factor-times-zero-plus-one path; its output scales with gains.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/style_demod_toy.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  auto t      = n::DType::Float64;
  auto x      = n::tensor({1., 0.}, {1, 1, 1, 2}, t);
  auto w      = n::tensor({3., 4.}, {1, 1, 2, 1}, t).requires_grad_();
  auto o      = n::modulated_conv2d(x, w, n::ones({1, 2}, t));
  auto dw     = n::grad(n::sum(o.image), {w})[0];
  if (std::abs(dw.at({0, 0, 0, 0}) - .128) > 1e-9 || std::abs(dw.at({0, 0, 1, 0}) + .096) > 1e-9)
    throw std::runtime_error("live normalization partials");
  std::vector<double> gain, demodulated, rgb;
  for (int i = 1; i <= 40; ++i) {
    double a = .05 * i;
    auto   s = n::full({1, 2}, a, t);
    gain.push_back(a);
    demodulated.push_back(n::modulated_conv2d(x, w, s).image.item());
    rgb.push_back(n::modulated_conv2d(x, w, s, false).image.item());
  }
  auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  p.y_limits(-.2, 8)
      .lines(gain, demodulated, "Demodulated", {37, 99, 235}, 2)
      .lines(gain, rgb, "RGB: no demodulation", {220, 38, 38}, 2)
      .x_label("Common positive factor applied to both channel gains")
      .y_label("1x1 output for supplied input(1,0)")
      .title("Feature kernels normalize scale; RGB preserves scale")
      .save_svg("build/style_demod_toy.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
\image(figures/style_demod_toy.svg)
// result_end
\caption(All40 factors from.05 through2 are retained. Positive common scaling cancels up to epsilon in the demodulated map; the RGB control changes from.15 to6. Zero and negative gains are supported separately by the primitive tests.)
\alttext(A nearly flat.6 demodulated curve and rising non-demodulated curve compare40 common style factors.)

> Zero noise strength blocks noise initially, while the strength can learn

The source initializes each four-channel noise strength to zero. Thus changing
supplied spatial noise initially changes no output bits and the noise-input
partial is zero. The strength partial need not be zero: for h=base+strength*noise,
at strength0 the derivative with respect to strength is noise. This supplied
four-position example has sum(noise)=10. The full model tests check the same
property through both styled generators, and show that nonzero strengths restore
noise-input derivatives. Noise is never sampled secretly inside synthesis.

```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n   = dm::nn;
  auto t        = n::DType::Float64;
  auto noise    = n::tensor({1., 2., 3., 4.}, {1, 2, 2, 1}, t).requires_grad_();
  auto strength = n::zeros({1}, t).requires_grad_();
  auto loss     = n::sum(n::ones(noise.shape(), t) + noise * strength);
  auto partial  = n::grad(loss, {noise, strength});
  if (n::max(n::abs(partial[0])).item() != 0 || partial[1].item() != 10)
    throw std::runtime_error("learnable zero strength");
  std::print(
      "| Supplied control | Partial |\n|---|---:|\n| max absolute noise-input partial at strength0 "
      "| {} |\n| strength partial at strength0 | {} |\n",
      n::max(n::abs(partial[0])).item(),
      partial[1].item());
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
| Supplied control | Partial |
|---|---:|
| max absolute noise-input partial at strength0 | 0 |
| strength partial at strength0 | 10 |
// result_end
> Preserve the least-squares loss scales and fresh-generator schedule

D minimizes.5 times the sum of the real-to1 and fake-to0 mean squares. G
minimizes the full fake-to1 mean square, with no half. At zero scores D=.5,
G=1; at fake score.25 the G partial is2*(.25-1)=-1.5. Real and fake pools
may have different row counts; means stay separate. During fitting each critic
capture/write precedes a fresh generator forward through the updated critic,
using the same latent/noise batch. Each optimizer owns one store alone.

```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  auto t      = n::DType::Float64;
  auto real = n::zeros({2, 1}, t), fake = n::full({3, 1}, .25, t).requires_grad_();
  auto d       = .5 * (n::mean(n::square(real - 1.)) + n::mean(n::square(fake)));
  auto g       = n::mean(n::square(fake - 1.));
  auto partial = n::grad(g, {fake})[0];
  if (d.item() != .53125 || g.item() != .5625 || n::sum(partial).item() != -1.5)
    throw std::runtime_error("loss scales");
  std::print(
      "| Supplied score control | Value |\n|---|---:|\n| D loss | {} |\n| G loss | {} |\n| sum of "
      "fake-score G partials | {} |\n",
      d.item(),
      g.item(),
      n::sum(partial).item());
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
| Supplied score control | Value |
|---|---:|
| D loss | 0.53125 |
| G loss | 0.5625 |
| sum of fake-score G partials | -1.5 |
// result_end
> Trace both actual generator paths

Mapping uses pixel RMS normalization followed by two dense8/LeakyReLU(.2)
layers:144 values in four leaves. A learned[1,4,4,4] constant is tiled per row.
AdaIN uses plain3x3 convolution, noise/bias, leaky activation, population spatial
normalization, then affine scale/shift. The modulated path learns affine(W)+1
channel gains and demodulates each row's feature kernel; there is no AdaIN.
Its1x1 RGB uses W1 with no demodulation. All kernels use source initialization;
noise strengths and biases start zero. The executed traces call the canonical
APIs and expose actual constant, mapped styles, noise and synthesis boundaries.
For the single-input plotting interface only, each trace packs Z8,noise4(16) and
noise8(64) into an88-value supplied input, then slices them explicitly. Synthesis
still uses the separate native arguments; no additional learned leaves are added.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/style_adain_architecture.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  namespace m = n::models;
  n::ParameterStore g(6607);
  n::Module         model(
      [&](const n::Tensor& packed) {
        auto z  = n::slice(packed, {0, 0}, {1, 8});
        auto n4 = n::reshape(n::slice(packed, {0, 8}, {1, 16}), {1, 4, 4, 1});
        auto n8 = n::reshape(n::slice(packed, {0, 24}, {1, 64}), {1, 8, 8, 1});
        n::model_stage("Supplied Z8", packed, z);
        n::model_stage("Supplied noise4", packed, n4);
        n::model_stage("Supplied noise8", packed, n8);
        auto w = m::StyleGanMap(g, z);
        n::model_stage("Pixel RMS + dense8/leaky x2", z, w);
        auto o = m::StyleGanSynthesize(g, w, w, n4, n8, false);
        n::model_stage("Tile learned constant", g.at("constant"), o.tiled_constant);
        n::model_stage(
            "Styled4 + supplied noise4", std::vector<n::Tensor>{o.tiled_constant, w, n4}, o.first);
        n::model_stage("Nearest up2", o.first, o.upsampled);
        n::model_stage(
            "Styled8 + supplied noise8", std::vector<n::Tensor>{o.upsampled, w, n8}, o.second);
        return n::model_stage("RGB sigmoid", std::vector<n::Tensor>{o.second, w}, o.image);
      },
      "adain compact generator");
  n::ModelPlotOptions options;
  options.style                 = n::ModelPlotStyle::Flow;
  options.detail                = n::ModelPlotDetail::Blocks;
  options.sizing.minimum_extent = 2;
  options.sizing.max_planes     = 4;
  auto figure                   = model.plot(n::ones({1, 88}), options);
  if (figure.parameter_count() != 661 || g.size() != 17)
    throw std::runtime_error("executed source census");
  figure.save_svg("build/style_adain_architecture.svg");
}
```
