> AdaIN: keep all original generation and style/noise galleries

The generated grid contains the first40 held-out latent rows. Mixing rows use
columns: ordinary(W,W), second-layer mix(W,other_W), first-layer mix(other_W,W),
other_W at both layers, and changed spatial noise with the original W. Each row
is the same latent identity across columns; this does not make generated samples
paired with real digit targets. Noise is unchanged for all four style columns.

