// result_begin: markdown
\image(figures/style_adain_truncation_noise.png)
// result_end
\caption(AdaIN: Eight rows, columns psi1/.5/0 with shared first-row noise, ordinary with original per-row noise, and changed noise. Equal psi0 images require both common W and common noise.)
\alttext(An8-by5 grid compares three truncation levels with shared noise and two generation controls with per-row noise.)

Truncation uses a fresh2048-row prior bank(zseed6733) mapped through the final
G. Its center is computed as Double mean(W) then cast back to Float32; there is
no moving average. W_psi=center+psi*(W-center). The shared-noise truncation
columns repeat the first row's noise maps at every row; ordinary/changed-noise
columns retain their original per-row banks. A collapse at psi0 here describes
a controlled input condition, not a fitted model collapse.

> Modulated: keep all original generation and style/noise galleries

The generated grid contains the first40 held-out latent rows. Mixing rows use
columns: ordinary(W,W), second-layer mix(W,other_W), first-layer mix(other_W,W),
other_W at both layers, and changed spatial noise with the original W. Each row
is the same latent identity across columns; this does not make generated samples
paired with real digit targets. Noise is unchanged for all four style columns.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/style_modulated_generated.png", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
namespace n = dm::nn;
namespace m = n::models;
using A     = std::map<std::string, n::Tensor>;
A Read(const std::string& path) {
  A a;
  for (const auto& [key, value] : n::load_npz(path))
    a.emplace(key, value);
  return a;
}
int main() {
  std::filesystem::copy_file(
      "build/style_gan/modulated/generated.png",
      "build/style_modulated_generated.png",
      std::filesystem::copy_options::overwrite_existing);
}
